{"content_text": "{\"protocolSection\":{\"identificationModule\":{\"nctId\":\"NCT02591862\",\"orgStudyIdInfo\":{\"id\":\"AK578\"},\"organization\":{\"fullName\":\"AKARI Therapeutics\",\"class\":\"INDUSTRY\"},\"briefTitle\":\"Coversin in Paroxysmal Nocturnal Haemoglobinuria (PNH)\",\"officialTitle\":\"Coversin in Paroxysmal Nocturnal Haemoglobinuria (PNH) in Patients With Resistance to Eculizumab Due to Complement C5 Polymorphisms\"},\"statusModule\":{\"statusVerifiedDate\":\"2017-02\",\"overallStatus\":\"COMPLETED\",\"expandedAccessInfo\":{\"hasExpandedAccess\":false},\"startDateStruct\":{\"date\":\"2016-02\",\"type\":\"ACTUAL\"},\"primaryCompletionDateStruct\":{\"date\":\"2018-03-20\",\"type\":\"ACTUAL\"},\"completionDateStruct\":{\"date\":\"2018-03-20\",\"type\":\"ACTUAL\"},\"studyFirstSubmitDate\":\"2015-09-10\",\"studyFirstSubmitQcDate\":\"2015-10-29\",\"studyFirstPostDateStruct\":{\"date\":\"2015-10-30\",\"type\":\"ESTIMATED\"},\"resultsFirstSubmitDate\":\"2021-08-13\",\"resultsFirstSubmitQcDate\":\"2023-06-20\",\"resultsFirstPostDateStruct\":{\"date\":\"2023-07-12\",\"type\":\"ACTUAL\"},\"lastUpdateSubmitDate\":\"2023-06-20\",\"lastUpdatePostDateStruct\":{\"date\":\"2023-07-12\",\"type\":\"ACTUAL\"}},\"sponsorCollaboratorsModule\":{\"responsibleParty\":{\"type\":\"SPONSOR\"},\"leadSponsor\":{\"name\":\"AKARI Therapeutics\",\"class\":\"INDUSTRY\"},\"collaborators\":[{\"name\":\"Radboud University Medical Center\",\"class\":\"OTHER\"}]},\"oversightModule\":{\"oversightHasDmc\":true},\"descriptionModule\":{\"briefSummary\":\"Coversin in Paroxysmal Nocturnal Haemoglobinuria (PNH) in patients with resistance to Eculizumab due to complement C5 polymorphisms.\",\"detailedDescription\":\"Coversin, a small protein complement C5 inhibitor which prevents the cleavage of C5 by C5 convertase into C5a and C5b, will be used in an open label, non-comparative clinical trial in patients with PNH and proven resistance to eculizumab due to C5 polymorphisms. Patients will be treated with Coversin by daily subcutaneous injection for 6 months in order to determine the safety and efficacy of the drug in these circumstances. If satisfactory control of the PNH is achieved, and at the discretion of the Principal Investigator (PI), patients will have the option of remaining on Coversin and being entered into the long term follow-up study for 2 years.\\n\\nPlease note, 'Coversin' is used throughout, but Nomacopan is the official name/INN.\\n\\nPlease note, the end points were assessed for 6 months, but the adverse events were measured over the 2 year period.\"},\"conditionsModule\":{\"conditions\":[\"Paroxysmal Nocturnal Haemoglobinuria (PNH)\"]},\"designModule\":{\"studyType\":\"INTERVENTIONAL\",\"phases\":[\"PHASE2\"],\"designInfo\":{\"allocation\":\"NA\",\"interventionModel\":\"SINGLE_GROUP\",\"primaryPurpose\":\"TREATMENT\",\"maskingInfo\":{\"masking\":\"NONE\"}},\"enrollmentInfo\":{\"count\":1,\"type\":\"ACTUAL\"}},\"armsInterventionsModule\":{\"armGroups\":[{\"label\":\"Coversin (Nomacopan)\",\"type\":\"OTHER\",\"description\":\"This is an open label, non-comparator study.\\n\\nPatient will be given a single ablating dose of 0.57mg/kg per subject followed by daily repeat maintenance doses. The initial repeat dose will be 25% of the ablating dose. If this is insufficient to maintain complement inhibition at ≤10% of baseline (pre-treatment) level after 5 days of treatment the daily dose will be increased by doubling until that level of inhibition is achieved. In the event of 100% inhibition being achieved the dose may be titrated downwards at the PI's discretion until a satisfactory clinical result is obtained. If at any point in treatment complement inhibition falls to less than 50% of baseline a further ablating dose of 0.57mg/kg should be given. Coversin lyophilised powder in each vial was diluted with 0.6 mL water for injection prior to use.\",\"interventionNames\":[\"Drug: Coversin\"]}],\"interventions\":[{\"type\":\"DRUG\",\"name\":\"Coversin\",\"description\":\"Patients enrolled in this protocol will initially be treated with an ablating dose of Coversin and daily repeat maintenance doses calculated according to body weight, the ablating dose to be 0.57mg/kg. Thereafter the daily repeat dose will be titrated according to clinical response and complement inhibition determined by CH50 ELISA. The initial repeat dose will be 25% of the ablating dose and this will be adjusted up or down if necessary once steady state is reached (5 days).\",\"armGroupLabels\":[\"Coversin (Nomacopan)\"],\"otherNames\":[\"rVA576\",\"rEV576\"]}]},\"outcomesModule\":{\"primaryOutcomes\":[{\"measure\":\"Measurement of Ratio of LDH to the Upper Limit of Normal (ULN)\",\"description\":\"LDH is an indicator of disease progression in patients with PNH and is expected to fall to within 2x upper limit of normal (ULN) within 28 days in successfully treated patients. Units are measured in ratio of LDH:ULN, where the ULN is 250 U/L. The primary efficacy endpoint was the LDH AUC from Day 0 to 28 compared with 28 days pretreatment. Data for the 28 days pre-treatment was not collected, and as only one patient was recruited, the LDH values compared with baseline and the ratio of LDH to the Upper Limit of Normal (ULN) are presented.\",\"timeFrame\":\"Day 0 and Day 28\"},{\"measure\":\"Number and Type of Adverse Events (AE)\",\"description\":\"The number and type of reported AEs will be recorded as well as the opinion of the Principle Investigator (PI) as to their possible relationship to the study drug.\",\"timeFrame\":\"2 years\"}],\"secondaryOutcomes\":[{\"measure\":\"Measurement of Haemoglobin (Hb) at Days 28, 90, and 180, Absolute and Change From Baseline\",\"description\":\"Measuring change in mean Hb from Day 28, Day 90 and Day 180 (absolute and change from baseline)\",\"timeFrame\":\"Baseline, Day 28, Day 90 and Day 180\"},{\"measure\":\"Measurement of Haptoglobin (Hp) at Days 28, 90 and 180, Absolute and Change From Baseline\",\"description\":\"Measuring change in mean Hp from Day 28, Day 90 and Day 180 (absolute and change from baseline)\",\"timeFrame\":\"Baseline, Day 28, Day 90 and Day 180\"},{\"measure\":\"Measurement of Lactate Dehydrogenase (LDH) at Baseline, Day 90 and Day 180\",\"description\":\"Measuring the change in LDH at Baseline, Day 90 and Day 180. LDH is an indicator of disease progression in patients with PNH and is expected to fall to within 2x upper limit of normal (ULN) within 28 days in successfully treated patients. Units are measured in ratio of LDH:ULN, where the ULN is 250 U/L.\",\"timeFrame\":\"Baseline, Day 90 and Day 180\"},{\"measure\":\"Change in Functional Assessment of Chronic Illness Therapy (FACIT) Score at Days 0, 28, 90 and 180\",\"description\":\"Functional Assessment of Chronic Illness Therapy - fatigue (FACIT-F) is a 13 item instrument designed to assess fatigue/tiredness and it's impact on daily activities and functioning in a chronic disease setting. The scale for each question in relation to quality of life ranges from 0-4 where 0= not at all, 1= a little bit, 2= somewhat, 3 = quite a bit and 4= very much. An increase in the scale score indicates an improvement in quality of life (less fatigue). A maximum score of 52 is interpreted as no fatigue . Baseline is assumed as 0.0 to demonstrate the change in units.\\n\\nThe subscale score (as presented) is determined as per FACIT-f guidance, by multiplying the sum of the item scores by the number of items in the subscale, then divide by the number of items answered.\",\"timeFrame\":\"Day 28, 90 and 180\"},{\"measure\":\"Change in Quality Of Life Questionnaire (QOQ) Score at Days 0, 28, 90 and 180\",\"description\":\"The European Organization for Research and Treatment of Cancer (EORTC) Quality of Life Questionnaire (QLQ)-C30 instrument measures the change in the quality of of life of patients in the trial. It comprises 30 questions on daily QOL and incorporates a global health status, five functional scales (physical, role, cognitive, emotional and social), three symptom scales (fatigue, nausea/vomiting, pain), and six single items (dyspnoea, insomnia, appetite loss, constipation, diarrhoea, financial difficulties). All of the scales range in score from 0 to 100, A high scale score represents a higher response level. Thus a high score for a functional scale represents a high / healthy level of functioning, a high score for the global health status / QoL represents a high QoL, but a high score for a symptom scale / item represents a high level of symptomatology / problems. Scale scores were calculated by averaging items within scales and transforming average scores linearly.\",\"timeFrame\":\"Day 28, 90 and 180\"},{\"measure\":\"Dependency on Blood Transfusion\",\"description\":\"Number of participants depending on blood transfusion prior to starting the study compared to during the study.\",\"timeFrame\":\"Day 0 through to study completion (2 years)\"}]},\"eligibilityModule\":{\"eligibilityCriteria\":\"Inclusion Criteria:\\n\\n* Patients with known Paroxysmal Nocturnal Haemoglobinuria (PNH)\\n* LDH \\\\>=1.5 Upper Limit of Normal (ULN)\\n* Resistance to Eculizumab proven by both a recognised C5 polymorphism on genetic screening and complement inhibition on CH50 ELISA of \\\\<100% at concentrations of Eculizumab in excess of 50 μg/mL\\n* Willing to self-inject Coversin daily or to receive daily subcutaneous injections by a home nurse or in a doctor's office or hospital clinic\\n* Males or females taking adequate contraceptive precautions if of childbearing potential, 18 - 80 years of age\\n* Body weight ≥50kg and ≤ 100kg\\n* The patient has provided written informed consent.\\n* Willing to avoid prohibited medications for duration of study\\n* Must agree to take appropriate prophylactic precautions against Neisseria infection.\\n* Must be counselled regarding the possible reproductive risks of using Coversin and be advised to use an adequate method of contraception pending further data on reproductive toxicology.\\n\\nExclusion Criteria:\\n\\n* Body weight \\\\<50kg or\\\\>100kg\\n* Pregnancy (females)\\n* Failure to satisfy the PI of fitness to participate for any other reason\\n* Known allergy to ticks or severe reaction to arthropod venom (e.g., bee or wasp venom)\",\"healthyVolunteers\":false,\"sex\":\"ALL\",\"minimumAge\":\"18 Years\",\"maximumAge\":\"80 Years\",\"stdAges\":[\"ADULT\",\"OLDER_ADULT\"]},\"contactsLocationsModule\":{\"overallOfficials\":[{\"name\":\"Petra Dr Muus\",\"affiliation\":\"Radboud University Medical Center\",\"role\":\"PRINCIPAL_INVESTIGATOR\"},{\"name\":\"Saskia Dr Langemeijer\",\"affiliation\":\"Radboud University Medical Center\",\"role\":\"STUDY_DIRECTOR\"}],\"locations\":[{\"facility\":\"Dr Saskia Langemeijer\",\"city\":\"Nijmegen\",\"zip\":\"6525 GA\",\"country\":\"Netherlands\",\"geoPoint\":{\"lat\":51.8425,\"lon\":5.85278}}]},\"referencesModule\":{\"references\":[{\"pmid\":\"31840801\",\"type\":\"RESULT\",\"citation\":\"Schols S, Nunn MA, Mackie I, Weston-Davies W, Nishimura JI, Kanakura Y, Blijlevens N, Muus P, Langemeijer S. Successful treatment of a PNH patient non-responsive to eculizumab with the novel complement C5 inhibitor coversin (nomacopan). Br J Haematol. 2020 Jan;188(2):334-337. doi: 10.1111/bjh.16305. Epub 2019 Dec 16. No abstract available.\"}],\"seeAlsoLinks\":[{\"label\":\"Successful treatment of a PNH patient non-responsive to eculizumab with the novel complement C5 inhibitor coversin (nomacopan)\",\"url\":\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31840801/\"}]}},\"resultsSection\":{\"participantFlowModule\":{\"groups\":[{\"id\":\"FG000\",\"title\":\"Coversin\",\"description\":\"This is an open label, non-comparator study.\\n\\nPatient will be given a single ablating dose of 0.57mg/kg per subject followed by daily repeat maintenance doses. The initial repeat dose will be 25% of the ablating dose. If this is insufficient to maintain complement inhibition at ≤10% of baseline (pre-treatment) level after 5 days of treatment the daily dose will be increased by doubling until that level of inhibition is achieved. In the event of 100% inhibition being achieved the dose may be titrated downwards at the PI's discretion until a satisfactory clinical result is obtained. If at any point in treatment complement inhibition falls to less than 50% of baseline a further ablating dose of 0.57mg/kg should be given.\\n\\nCoversin: Patients enrolled in this protocol will initially be treated with an ablating dose of Coversin and daily repeat maintenance doses calculated according to body weight, the ablating dose to be 0.57mg/kg. Thereafter the daily repeat dose will be titrated according to clinical response and complement inhibition determined by CH50 ELISA. The initial repeat dose will be 25% of the ablating dose and this will be adjusted up or down if necessary once steady state is reached (5 days).\"}],\"periods\":[{\"title\":\"Overall Study\",\"milestones\":[{\"type\":\"STARTED\",\"achievements\":[{\"groupId\":\"FG000\",\"numSubjects\":\"1\"}]},{\"type\":\"COMPLETED\",\"achievements\":[{\"groupId\":\"FG000\",\"numSubjects\":\"1\"}]},{\"type\":\"NOT COMPLETED\",\"achievements\":[{\"groupId\":\"FG000\",\"numSubjects\":\"0\"}]}]}]},\"baselineCharacteristicsModule\":{\"groups\":[{\"id\":\"BG000\",\"title\":\"Coversin\",\"description\":\"This is an open label, non-comparator study.\\n\\nPatient will be given a single ablating dose of 0.57mg/kg per subject followed by daily repeat maintenance doses. The initial repeat dose will be 25% of the ablating dose. If this is insufficient to maintain complement inhibition at ≤10% of baseline (pre-treatment) level after 5 days of treatment the daily dose will be increased by doubling until that level of inhibition is achieved. In the event of 100% inhibition being achieved the dose may be titrated downwards at the PI's discretion until a satisfactory clinical result is obtained. If at any point in treatment complement inhibition falls to less than 50% of baseline a further ablating dose of 0.57mg/kg should be given.\\n\\nCoversin: Patients enrolled in this protocol will initially be treated with an ablating dose of Coversin and daily repeat maintenance doses calculated according to body weight, the ablating dose to be 0.57mg/kg. Thereafter the daily repeat dose will be titrated according to clinical response and complement inhibition determined by CH50 ELISA. The initial repeat dose will be 25% of the ablating dose and this will be adjusted up or down if necessary once steady state is reached (5 days).\"}],\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"1\"}]}],\"measures\":[{\"title\":\"Age, Categorical\",\"paramType\":\"COUNT_OF_PARTICIPANTS\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"Participants\",\"classes\":[{\"categories\":[{\"title\":\"<=18 years\",\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"0\"}]},{\"title\":\"Between 18 and 65 years\",\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"1\"}]},{\"title\":\">=65 years\",\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"0\"}]}]}]},{\"title\":\"Age, Continuous\",\"paramType\":\"MEAN\",\"dispersionType\":\"STANDARD_DEVIATION\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"years\",\"classes\":[{\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"32\",\"spread\":\"0\"}]}]}]},{\"title\":\"Sex: Female, Male\",\"paramType\":\"COUNT_OF_PARTICIPANTS\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"Participants\",\"classes\":[{\"categories\":[{\"title\":\"Female\",\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"0\"}]},{\"title\":\"Male\",\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"1\"}]}]}]},{\"title\":\"Race (NIH/OMB)\",\"paramType\":\"COUNT_OF_PARTICIPANTS\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"Participants\",\"classes\":[{\"categories\":[{\"title\":\"American Indian or Alaska Native\",\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"0\"}]},{\"title\":\"Asian\",\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"0\"}]},{\"title\":\"Native Hawaiian or Other Pacific Islander\",\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"0\"}]},{\"title\":\"Black or African American\",\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"0\"}]},{\"title\":\"White\",\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"1\"}]},{\"title\":\"More than one race\",\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"0\"}]},{\"title\":\"Unknown or Not Reported\",\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"0\"}]}]}]},{\"title\":\"Region of Enrollment\",\"paramType\":\"NUMBER\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"participants\",\"classes\":[{\"title\":\"Netherlands\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"1\"}]}]}]},{\"title\":\"Weight\",\"paramType\":\"NUMBER\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"kg\",\"classes\":[{\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"67.8\"}]}]}]},{\"title\":\"Height\",\"paramType\":\"NUMBER\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"cm\",\"classes\":[{\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"172\"}]}]}]},{\"title\":\"Serum Lactate Dehydrogenase\",\"paramType\":\"NUMBER\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"U/L\",\"classes\":[{\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"1391\"}]}]}]},{\"title\":\"Haemoglobin concentration (Hb)\",\"paramType\":\"NUMBER\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"Millimole(s)/litre\",\"classes\":[{\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"8.2\"}]}]}]},{\"title\":\"Haptoglobin (Hp) concentration\",\"paramType\":\"NUMBER\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"Gram(s)/litre\",\"classes\":[{\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"0.0\"}]}]}]},{\"title\":\"Dependency on blood transfusion\",\"paramType\":\"NUMBER\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"participants\",\"classes\":[{\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"0\"}]}]}]}]},\"outcomeMeasuresModule\":{\"outcomeMeasures\":[{\"type\":\"PRIMARY\",\"title\":\"Measurement of Ratio of LDH to the Upper Limit of Normal (ULN)\",\"description\":\"LDH is an indicator of disease progression in patients with PNH and is expected to fall to within 2x upper limit of normal (ULN) within 28 days in successfully treated patients. Units are measured in ratio of LDH:ULN, where the ULN is 250 U/L. The primary efficacy endpoint was the LDH AUC from Day 0 to 28 compared with 28 days pretreatment. Data for the 28 days pre-treatment was not collected, and as only one patient was recruited, the LDH values compared with baseline and the ratio of LDH to the Upper Limit of Normal (ULN) are presented.\",\"populationDescription\":\"Single arm trial design, results from 1 enrolled participant.\",\"reportingStatus\":\"POSTED\",\"paramType\":\"NUMBER\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"Ratio of LDH:ULN (250 U/L)\",\"timeFrame\":\"Day 0 and Day 28\",\"groups\":[{\"id\":\"OG000\",\"title\":\"Coversin\",\"description\":\"This is an open label, non-comparator study.\\n\\nPatient will be given a single ablating dose of 0.57mg/kg per subject followed by daily repeat maintenance doses. The initial repeat dose will be 25% of the ablating dose. If this is insufficient to maintain complement inhibition at ≤10% of baseline (pre-treatment) level after 5 days of treatment the daily dose will be increased by doubling until that level of inhibition is achieved. In the event of 100% inhibition being achieved the dose may be titrated downwards at the PI's discretion until a satisfactory clinical result is obtained. If at any point in treatment complement inhibition falls to less than 50% of baseline a further ablating dose of 0.57mg/kg should be given.\\n\\nCoversin : Patients enrolled in this protocol will initially be treated with an ablating dose of Coversin and daily repeat maintenance doses calculated according to body weight, the ablating dose to be 0.57mg/kg. Thereafter the daily repeat dose will be titrated according to clinical response and complement inhibition determined by CH50 ELISA. The initial repeat dose will be 25% of the ablating dose and this will be adjusted up or down if necessary once steady state is reached (5 days).\"}],\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"1\"}]}],\"classes\":[{\"title\":\"Day 0\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"5.6\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Day 28\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"1.9\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"PRIMARY\",\"title\":\"Number and Type of Adverse Events (AE)\",\"description\":\"The number and type of reported AEs will be recorded as well as the opinion of the Principle Investigator (PI) as to their possible relationship to the study drug.\",\"populationDescription\":\"Results from 1 enrolled participant.\",\"reportingStatus\":\"POSTED\",\"paramType\":\"NUMBER\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"Events\",\"timeFrame\":\"2 years\",\"groups\":[{\"id\":\"OG000\",\"title\":\"Coversin\",\"description\":\"This is an open label, non-comparator study.\\n\\nPatient will be given a single ablating dose of 0.57mg/kg per subject followed by daily repeat maintenance doses. The initial repeat dose will be 25% of the ablating dose. If this is insufficient to maintain complement inhibition at ≤10% of baseline (pre-treatment) level after 5 days of treatment the daily dose will be increased by doubling until that level of inhibition is achieved. In the event of 100% inhibition being achieved the dose may be titrated downwards at the PI's discretion until a satisfactory clinical result is obtained. If at any point in treatment complement inhibition falls to less than 50% of baseline a further ablating dose of 0.57mg/kg should be given.\\n\\nCoversin : Patients enrolled in this protocol will initially be treated with an ablating dose of Coversin and daily repeat maintenance doses calculated according to body weight, the ablating dose to be 0.57mg/kg. Thereafter the daily repeat dose will be titrated according to clinical response and complement inhibition determined by CH50 ELISA. The initial repeat dose will be 25% of the ablating dose and this will be adjusted up or down if necessary once steady state is reached (5 days).\"}],\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"1\"}]}],\"classes\":[{\"title\":\"Serious Adverse Events (SAE)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"2\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Adverse Event (AE) (total)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"20\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Treatment Emergent Adverse Event (TAEA)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"13\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"AE - moderate\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"1\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"AE - severe\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"1\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"AE- mild\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"18\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"SECONDARY\",\"title\":\"Measurement of Haemoglobin (Hb) at Days 28, 90, and 180, Absolute and Change From Baseline\",\"description\":\"Measuring change in mean Hb from Day 28, Day 90 and Day 180 (absolute and change from baseline)\",\"populationDescription\":\"Results from 1 enrolled participant.\",\"reportingStatus\":\"POSTED\",\"paramType\":\"NUMBER\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"millimole(s)/litre\",\"timeFrame\":\"Baseline, Day 28, Day 90 and Day 180\",\"groups\":[{\"id\":\"OG000\",\"title\":\"Coversin\",\"description\":\"This is an open label, non-comparator study.\\n\\nPatient will be given a single ablating dose of 0.57mg/kg per subject followed by daily repeat maintenance doses. The initial repeat dose will be 25% of the ablating dose. If this is insufficient to maintain complement inhibition at ≤10% of baseline (pre-treatment) level after 5 days of treatment the daily dose will be increased by doubling until that level of inhibition is achieved. In the event of 100% inhibition being achieved the dose may be titrated downwards at the PI's discretion until a satisfactory clinical result is obtained. If at any point in treatment complement inhibition falls to less than 50% of baseline a further ablating dose of 0.57mg/kg should be given.\\n\\nCoversin : Patients enrolled in this protocol will initially be treated with an ablating dose of Coversin and daily repeat maintenance doses calculated according to body weight, the ablating dose to be 0.57mg/kg. Thereafter the daily repeat dose will be titrated according to clinical response and complement inhibition determined by CH50 ELISA. The initial repeat dose will be 25% of the ablating dose and this will be adjusted up or down if necessary once steady state is reached (5 days).\"}],\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"1\"}]}],\"classes\":[{\"title\":\"Baseline\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"8.2\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Day 28 (absolute)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"7.8\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Day 28 (change from baseline)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"-0.7\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Day 90 (absolute)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"7.8\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Day 90 (change from baseline)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"-0.4\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Day 180 (absolute)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"8.0\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Day 180 (change from baseline)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"-0.2\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"SECONDARY\",\"title\":\"Measurement of Haptoglobin (Hp) at Days 28, 90 and 180, Absolute and Change From Baseline\",\"description\":\"Measuring change in mean Hp from Day 28, Day 90 and Day 180 (absolute and change from baseline)\",\"populationDescription\":\"Results from 1 enrolled participant.\",\"reportingStatus\":\"POSTED\",\"paramType\":\"NUMBER\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"gram(s)/litre\",\"timeFrame\":\"Baseline, Day 28, Day 90 and Day 180\",\"groups\":[{\"id\":\"OG000\",\"title\":\"Coversin\",\"description\":\"This is an open label, non-comparator study.\\n\\nPatient will be given a single ablating dose of 0.57mg/kg per subject followed by daily repeat maintenance doses. The initial repeat dose will be 25% of the ablating dose. If this is insufficient to maintain complement inhibition at ≤10% of baseline (pre-treatment) level after 5 days of treatment the daily dose will be increased by doubling until that level of inhibition is achieved. In the event of 100% inhibition being achieved the dose may be titrated downwards at the PI's discretion until a satisfactory clinical result is obtained. If at any point in treatment complement inhibition falls to less than 50% of baseline a further ablating dose of 0.57mg/kg should be given.\\n\\nCoversin : Patients enrolled in this protocol will initially be treated with an ablating dose of Coversin and daily repeat maintenance doses calculated according to body weight, the ablating dose to be 0.57mg/kg. Thereafter the daily repeat dose will be titrated according to clinical response and complement inhibition determined by CH50 ELISA. The initial repeat dose will be 25% of the ablating dose and this will be adjusted up or down if necessary once steady state is reached (5 days).\"}],\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"1\"}]}],\"classes\":[{\"title\":\"Baseline\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"NA\",\"comment\":\"Haptoglobin was undetectable\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Day 28\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"NA\",\"comment\":\"Haptoglobin was undetectable\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Day 90\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"NA\",\"comment\":\"Haptoglobin was undetectable\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Day 180\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"NA\",\"comment\":\"The assay failed on day 180\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"SECONDARY\",\"title\":\"Measurement of Lactate Dehydrogenase (LDH) at Baseline, Day 90 and Day 180\",\"description\":\"Measuring the change in LDH at Baseline, Day 90 and Day 180. LDH is an indicator of disease progression in patients with PNH and is expected to fall to within 2x upper limit of normal (ULN) within 28 days in successfully treated patients. Units are measured in ratio of LDH:ULN, where the ULN is 250 U/L.\",\"populationDescription\":\"Single arm trial design, results from 1 enrolled participant.\",\"reportingStatus\":\"POSTED\",\"paramType\":\"NUMBER\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"Ratio of LDH:ULN (250 U/L)\",\"timeFrame\":\"Baseline, Day 90 and Day 180\",\"groups\":[{\"id\":\"OG000\",\"title\":\"Coversin\",\"description\":\"This is an open label, non-comparator study.\\n\\nPatient will be given a single ablating dose of 0.57mg/kg per subject followed by daily repeat maintenance doses. The initial repeat dose will be 25% of the ablating dose. If this is insufficient to maintain complement inhibition at ≤10% of baseline (pre-treatment) level after 5 days of treatment the daily dose will be increased by doubling until that level of inhibition is achieved. In the event of 100% inhibition being achieved the dose may be titrated downwards at the PI's discretion until a satisfactory clinical result is obtained. If at any point in treatment complement inhibition falls to less than 50% of baseline a further ablating dose of 0.57mg/kg should be given.\\n\\nCoversin : Patients enrolled in this protocol will initially be treated with an ablating dose of Coversin and daily repeat maintenance doses calculated according to body weight, the ablating dose to be 0.57mg/kg. Thereafter the daily repeat dose will be titrated according to clinical response and complement inhibition determined by CH50 ELISA. The initial repeat dose will be 25% of the ablating dose and this will be adjusted up or down if necessary once steady state is reached (5 days).\"}],\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"1\"}]}],\"classes\":[{\"title\":\"Day 0\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"5.6\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Day 90\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"1.6\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Day 180\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"1.5\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"SECONDARY\",\"title\":\"Change in Functional Assessment of Chronic Illness Therapy (FACIT) Score at Days 0, 28, 90 and 180\",\"description\":\"Functional Assessment of Chronic Illness Therapy - fatigue (FACIT-F) is a 13 item instrument designed to assess fatigue/tiredness and it's impact on daily activities and functioning in a chronic disease setting. The scale for each question in relation to quality of life ranges from 0-4 where 0= not at all, 1= a little bit, 2= somewhat, 3 = quite a bit and 4= very much. An increase in the scale score indicates an improvement in quality of life (less fatigue). A maximum score of 52 is interpreted as no fatigue . Baseline is assumed as 0.0 to demonstrate the change in units.\\n\\nThe subscale score (as presented) is determined as per FACIT-f guidance, by multiplying the sum of the item scores by the number of items in the subscale, then divide by the number of items answered.\",\"reportingStatus\":\"POSTED\",\"paramType\":\"NUMBER\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"FACIT-f scale (Change from Baseline)\",\"timeFrame\":\"Day 28, 90 and 180\",\"groups\":[{\"id\":\"OG000\",\"title\":\"Coversin\",\"description\":\"This is an open label, non-comparator study.\\n\\nPatient will be given a single ablating dose of 0.57mg/kg per subject followed by daily repeat maintenance doses. The initial repeat dose will be 25% of the ablating dose. If this is insufficient to maintain complement inhibition at ≤10% of baseline (pre-treatment) level after 5 days of treatment the daily dose will be increased by doubling until that level of inhibition is achieved. In the event of 100% inhibition being achieved the dose may be titrated downwards at the PI's discretion until a satisfactory clinical result is obtained. If at any point in treatment complement inhibition falls to less than 50% of baseline a further ablating dose of 0.57mg/kg should be given. Coversin lyophilised powder in each vial was diluted with 0.6 mL water for injection prior to use.\\n\\nCoversin: Patients enrolled in this protocol will initially be treated with an ablating dose of Coversin and daily repeat maintenance doses calculated according to body weight, the ablating dose to be 0.57mg/kg. Thereafter the daily repeat dose will be titrated according to clinical response and complement inhibition determined by CH50 ELISA. The initial repeat dose will be 25% of the ablating dose and this will be adjusted up or down if necessary once steady state is reached (5 days).\"}],\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"1\"}]}],\"classes\":[{\"title\":\"Day 28\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"13.0\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Day 90\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"13.3\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Day 180\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"11.0\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"SECONDARY\",\"title\":\"Change in Quality Of Life Questionnaire (QOQ) Score at Days 0, 28, 90 and 180\",\"description\":\"The European Organization for Research and Treatment of Cancer (EORTC) Quality of Life Questionnaire (QLQ)-C30 instrument measures the change in the quality of of life of patients in the trial. It comprises 30 questions on daily QOL and incorporates a global health status, five functional scales (physical, role, cognitive, emotional and social), three symptom scales (fatigue, nausea/vomiting, pain), and six single items (dyspnoea, insomnia, appetite loss, constipation, diarrhoea, financial difficulties). All of the scales range in score from 0 to 100, A high scale score represents a higher response level. Thus a high score for a functional scale represents a high / healthy level of functioning, a high score for the global health status / QoL represents a high QoL, but a high score for a symptom scale / item represents a high level of symptomatology / problems. Scale scores were calculated by averaging items within scales and transforming average scores linearly.\",\"populationDescription\":\"Single arm trial design, results from 1 enrolled participant.\",\"reportingStatus\":\"POSTED\",\"paramType\":\"NUMBER\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"Scores on a scale (Change from baseline)\",\"timeFrame\":\"Day 28, 90 and 180\",\"groups\":[{\"id\":\"OG000\",\"title\":\"Coversin\",\"description\":\"This is an open label, non-comparator study.\\n\\nPatient will be given a single ablating dose of 0.57mg/kg per subject followed by daily repeat maintenance doses. The initial repeat dose will be 25% of the ablating dose. If this is insufficient to maintain complement inhibition at ≤10% of baseline (pre-treatment) level after 5 days of treatment the daily dose will be increased by doubling until that level of inhibition is achieved. In the event of 100% inhibition being achieved the dose may be titrated downwards at the PI's discretion until a satisfactory clinical result is obtained. If at any point in treatment complement inhibition falls to less than 50% of baseline a further ablating dose of 0.57mg/kg should be given. Coversin lyophilised powder in each vial was diluted with 0.6 mL water for injection prior to use.\\n\\nCoversin: Patients enrolled in this protocol will initially be treated with an ablating dose of Coversin and daily repeat maintenance doses calculated according to body weight, the ablating dose to be 0.57mg/kg. Thereafter the daily repeat dose will be titrated according to clinical response and complement inhibition determined by CH50 ELISA. The initial repeat dose will be 25% of the ablating dose and this will be adjusted up or down if necessary once steady state is reached (5 days).\"}],\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"1\"}]}],\"classes\":[{\"title\":\"Global Health Status/ QOL (day 28)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"16.7\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Global Health Status/ QOL (day 90)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"16.7\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Global Health Status/ QOL (day 180)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"16.7\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Physical Functioning (day 28)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"6.6\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Physical Functioning (day 90)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0.0\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Physical Functioning (day 180)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"6.6\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Role functioning (day 28)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"33.4\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Role functioning (day 90)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"33.4\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Role functioning (day 180)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"16.7\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Emotional functioning (day 28)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"16.6\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Emotional functioning (day 90)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"8.3\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Emotional functioning (day 180)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"8.3\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Cognitive functioning (day 28)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"33.3\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Cognitive functioning (day 90)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"16.7\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Cognitive functioning (day 180)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"16.7\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Social functioning (day 28)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0.0\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Social functioning (day 90)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0.0\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Social functioning (day 180)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0.0\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Fatigue symptom scale (day 28)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"-11.1\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Fatigue symptom scale (day 90)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0.0\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Fatigue symptom scale (day 180)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0.0\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Nausea and vomiting symptom scale (day 28)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0.0\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Nausea and vomiting symptom scale (day 90)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0.0\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Nausea and vomiting symptom scale (day 180)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0.0\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Pain symptom scale (day 28)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0.0\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Pain symptom scale (day 90)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"16.7\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Pain symptom scale (day 180)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0.0\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Symptom: Dyspnoea (day 28)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0.0\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Symptom: Dyspnoea (day 90)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0.0\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Symptom: Dyspnoea (day 180)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0.0\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Symptom: Insomnia (day 28)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"-33.3\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Symptom: Insomnia (day 90)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0.0\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Symptom: Insomnia (day 180)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0.0\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Symptom: Appetite loss (day 28)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0.0\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Symptom: Appetite loss (day 90)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0.0\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Symptom: Appetite loss (day 180)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0.0\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Symptom: constipation (day 28)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0.0\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Symptom: constipation (day 90)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0.0\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Symptom: constipation (day 180)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0.0\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Symptom: diarrhoea (day 28)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"-33.3\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Symptom: diarrhoea (day 90)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"-33.3\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Symptom: diarrhoea (day 180)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"-33.3\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Symptom: financial difficulties (day 28)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0.0\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Symptom: financial difficulties (day 90)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0.0\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Symptom: financial difficulties (day 190)\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0.0\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"SECONDARY\",\"title\":\"Dependency on Blood Transfusion\",\"description\":\"Number of participants depending on blood transfusion prior to starting the study compared to during the study.\",\"populationDescription\":\"Results from 1 enrolled participant.\",\"reportingStatus\":\"POSTED\",\"paramType\":\"NUMBER\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"participants\",\"timeFrame\":\"Day 0 through to study completion (2 years)\",\"groups\":[{\"id\":\"OG000\",\"title\":\"Coversin\",\"description\":\"This is an open label, non-comparator study.\\n\\nPatient will be given a single ablating dose of 0.57mg/kg per subject followed by daily repeat maintenance doses. The initial repeat dose will be 25% of the ablating dose. If this is insufficient to maintain complement inhibition at ≤10% of baseline (pre-treatment) level after 5 days of treatment the daily dose will be increased by doubling until that level of inhibition is achieved. In the event of 100% inhibition being achieved the dose may be titrated downwards at the PI's discretion until a satisfactory clinical result is obtained. If at any point in treatment complement inhibition falls to less than 50% of baseline a further ablating dose of 0.57mg/kg should be given.\\n\\nCoversin : Patients enrolled in this protocol will initially be treated with an ablating dose of Coversin and daily repeat maintenance doses calculated according to body weight, the ablating dose to be 0.57mg/kg. Thereafter the daily repeat dose will be titrated according to clinical response and complement inhibition determined by CH50 ELISA. The initial repeat dose will be 25% of the ablating dose and this will be adjusted up or down if necessary once steady state is reached (5 days).\"}],\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"1\"}]}],\"classes\":[{\"title\":\"Transfusion dependent prior to starting trial\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Transfusion dependent during trial\",\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0\"}]}]}]}]},\"adverseEventsModule\":{\"frequencyThreshold\":\"0\",\"timeFrame\":\"Duration of the study (2 years)\",\"eventGroups\":[{\"id\":\"EG000\",\"title\":\"Coversin\",\"description\":\"This is an open label, non-comparator study.\\n\\nPatient will be given a single ablating dose of 0.57mg/kg per subject followed by daily repeat maintenance doses. The initial repeat dose will be 25% of the ablating dose. If this is insufficient to maintain complement inhibition at ≤10% of baseline (pre-treatment) level after 5 days of treatment the daily dose will be increased by doubling until that level of inhibition is achieved. In the event of 100% inhibition being achieved the dose may be titrated downwards at the PI's discretion until a satisfactory clinical result is obtained. If at any point in treatment complement inhibition falls to less than 50% of baseline a further ablating dose of 0.57mg/kg should be given.\\n\\nCoversin: Patients enrolled in this protocol will initially be treated with an ablating dose of Coversin and daily repeat maintenance doses calculated according to body weight, the ablating dose to be 0.57mg/kg. Thereafter the daily repeat dose will be titrated according to clinical response and complement inhibition determined by CH50 ELISA. The initial repeat dose will be 25% of the ablating dose and this will be adjusted up or down if necessary once steady state is reached (5 days).\",\"deathsNumAffected\":0,\"deathsNumAtRisk\":1,\"seriousNumAffected\":1,\"seriousNumAtRisk\":1,\"otherNumAffected\":1,\"otherNumAtRisk\":1}],\"seriousEvents\":[{\"term\":\"Breakthrough Hemolysis\",\"organSystem\":\"Blood and lymphatic system disorders\",\"sourceVocabulary\":\"MedDRA (19.1)\",\"assessmentType\":\"SYSTEMATIC_ASSESSMENT\",\"stats\":[{\"groupId\":\"EG000\",\"numEvents\":1,\"numAffected\":1,\"numAtRisk\":1}]},{\"term\":\"Lung infection\",\"organSystem\":\"Infections and infestations\",\"sourceVocabulary\":\"MedDRA (19.1)\",\"assessmentType\":\"SYSTEMATIC_ASSESSMENT\",\"stats\":[{\"groupId\":\"EG000\",\"numEvents\":1,\"numAffected\":1,\"numAtRisk\":1}]}],\"otherEvents\":[{\"term\":\"Abdominal pain\",\"organSystem\":\"Gastrointestinal disorders\",\"sourceVocabulary\":\"MedDRA (19.1)\",\"assessmentType\":\"SYSTEMATIC_ASSESSMENT\",\"stats\":[{\"groupId\":\"EG000\",\"numEvents\":2,\"numAffected\":1,\"numAtRisk\":1}]},{\"term\":\"Nausea\",\"organSystem\":\"Gastrointestinal disorders\",\"sourceVocabulary\":\"MedDRA (19.1)\",\"assessmentType\":\"SYSTEMATIC_ASSESSMENT\",\"stats\":[{\"groupId\":\"EG000\",\"numEvents\":1,\"numAffected\":1,\"numAtRisk\":1}]},{\"term\":\"Cough\",\"organSystem\":\"General disorders\",\"sourceVocabulary\":\"MedDRA (19.1)\",\"assessmentType\":\"SYSTEMATIC_ASSESSMENT\",\"stats\":[{\"groupId\":\"EG000\",\"numEvents\":1,\"numAffected\":1,\"numAtRisk\":1}]},{\"term\":\"Fatigue\",\"organSystem\":\"General disorders\",\"sourceVocabulary\":\"MedDRA (19.1)\",\"assessmentType\":\"SYSTEMATIC_ASSESSMENT\",\"stats\":[{\"groupId\":\"EG000\",\"numEvents\":1,\"numAffected\":1,\"numAtRisk\":1}]},{\"term\":\"Flu like symptoms\",\"organSystem\":\"General disorders\",\"sourceVocabulary\":\"MedDRA (19.1)\",\"assessmentType\":\"SYSTEMATIC_ASSESSMENT\",\"stats\":[{\"groupId\":\"EG000\",\"numEvents\":5,\"numAffected\":1,\"numAtRisk\":1}]},{\"term\":\"Injection site Reaction\",\"organSystem\":\"General disorders\",\"sourceVocabulary\":\"MedDRA (19.1)\",\"assessmentType\":\"SYSTEMATIC_ASSESSMENT\",\"stats\":[{\"groupId\":\"EG000\",\"numEvents\":13,\"numAffected\":1,\"numAtRisk\":1}]},{\"term\":\"Malaise\",\"organSystem\":\"General disorders\",\"sourceVocabulary\":\"MedDRA (19.1)\",\"assessmentType\":\"SYSTEMATIC_ASSESSMENT\",\"stats\":[{\"groupId\":\"EG000\",\"numEvents\":2,\"numAffected\":1,\"numAtRisk\":1}]},{\"term\":\"Non-cardiac chest pain\",\"organSystem\":\"General disorders\",\"sourceVocabulary\":\"MedDRA (19.1)\",\"assessmentType\":\"SYSTEMATIC_ASSESSMENT\",\"stats\":[{\"groupId\":\"EG000\",\"numEvents\":1,\"numAffected\":1,\"numAtRisk\":1}]},{\"term\":\"Papulopustular rash\",\"organSystem\":\"Infections and infestations\",\"sourceVocabulary\":\"MedDRA (19.1)\",\"assessmentType\":\"SYSTEMATIC_ASSESSMENT\",\"stats\":[{\"groupId\":\"EG000\",\"numEvents\":1,\"numAffected\":1,\"numAtRisk\":1}]},{\"term\":\"Headache\",\"organSystem\":\"Nervous system disorders\",\"sourceVocabulary\":\"MedDRA (19.1)\",\"assessmentType\":\"SYSTEMATIC_ASSESSMENT\",\"stats\":[{\"groupId\":\"EG000\",\"numEvents\":6,\"numAffected\":1,\"numAtRisk\":1}]},{\"term\":\"Insomnia\",\"organSystem\":\"Nervous system disorders\",\"sourceVocabulary\":\"MedDRA (19.1)\",\"assessmentType\":\"SYSTEMATIC_ASSESSMENT\",\"stats\":[{\"groupId\":\"EG000\",\"numEvents\":1,\"numAffected\":1,\"numAtRisk\":1}]},{\"term\":\"Haematuria\",\"organSystem\":\"Renal and urinary disorders\",\"sourceVocabulary\":\"MedDRA (19.1)\",\"assessmentType\":\"SYSTEMATIC_ASSESSMENT\",\"stats\":[{\"groupId\":\"EG000\",\"numEvents\":1,\"numAffected\":1,\"numAtRisk\":1}]},{\"term\":\"Haemoglobinurea\",\"organSystem\":\"Renal and urinary disorders\",\"sourceVocabulary\":\"MedDRA (19.1)\",\"assessmentType\":\"SYSTEMATIC_ASSESSMENT\",\"stats\":[{\"groupId\":\"EG000\",\"numEvents\":1,\"numAffected\":1,\"numAtRisk\":1}]},{\"term\":\"Coughing\",\"organSystem\":\"Respiratory, thoracic and mediastinal disorders\",\"sourceVocabulary\":\"MedDRA (19.1)\",\"assessmentType\":\"SYSTEMATIC_ASSESSMENT\",\"stats\":[{\"groupId\":\"EG000\",\"numEvents\":1,\"numAffected\":1,\"numAtRisk\":1}]},{\"term\":\"Dyspnoea\",\"organSystem\":\"Respiratory, thoracic and mediastinal disorders\",\"sourceVocabulary\":\"MedDRA (19.1)\",\"assessmentType\":\"SYSTEMATIC_ASSESSMENT\",\"stats\":[{\"groupId\":\"EG000\",\"numEvents\":1,\"numAffected\":1,\"numAtRisk\":1}]},{\"term\":\"Sore throat\",\"organSystem\":\"Respiratory, thoracic and mediastinal disorders\",\"sourceVocabulary\":\"MedDRA (19.1)\",\"assessmentType\":\"SYSTEMATIC_ASSESSMENT\",\"stats\":[{\"groupId\":\"EG000\",\"numEvents\":2,\"numAffected\":1,\"numAtRisk\":1}]},{\"term\":\"Rash\",\"organSystem\":\"Skin and subcutaneous tissue disorders\",\"sourceVocabulary\":\"MedDRA (19.1)\",\"assessmentType\":\"SYSTEMATIC_ASSESSMENT\",\"stats\":[{\"groupId\":\"EG000\",\"numEvents\":1,\"numAffected\":1,\"numAtRisk\":1}]},{\"term\":\"Cold fingers and toes\",\"organSystem\":\"Vascular disorders\",\"sourceVocabulary\":\"MedDRA (19.1)\",\"assessmentType\":\"SYSTEMATIC_ASSESSMENT\",\"stats\":[{\"groupId\":\"EG000\",\"numEvents\":1,\"numAffected\":1,\"numAtRisk\":1}]}]},\"moreInfoModule\":{\"certainAgreement\":{\"piSponsorEmployee\":false,\"restrictionType\":\"OTHER\",\"restrictiveAgreement\":true,\"otherDetails\":\"The PI of the clinical units has independent rights of publication but will agree to discuss any intended publications or presentations with the Sponsor and to allow the Sponsor reasonable time to make comments, file or add to patent applications or request changes to the manuscript\"},\"pointOfContact\":{\"title\":\"Chief Scientific Officer\",\"organization\":\"Akari Therapeutics plc\",\"email\":\"miles.nunn@akaritx.com\",\"phone\":\"02080040261\"}}},\"documentSection\":{\"largeDocumentModule\":{\"largeDocs\":[{\"typeAbbrev\":\"Prot_SAP\",\"hasProtocol\":true,\"hasSap\":true,\"hasIcf\":false,\"label\":\"Study Protocol and Statistical Analysis Plan\",\"date\":\"2015-11-11\",\"uploadDate\":\"2021-08-12T10:47\",\"filename\":\"Prot_SAP_000.pdf\",\"size\":1013880}]}},\"derivedSection\":{\"miscInfoModule\":{\"versionHolder\":\"2026-09-18\"},\"conditionBrowseModule\":{\"meshes\":[{\"id\":\"D006457\",\"term\":\"Hemoglobinuria, Paroxysmal\"}],\"ancestors\":[{\"id\":\"D000743\",\"term\":\"Anemia, Hemolytic\"},{\"id\":\"D000740\",\"term\":\"Anemia\"},{\"id\":\"D006402\",\"term\":\"Hematologic Diseases\"},{\"id\":\"D006425\",\"term\":\"Hemic and Lymphatic Diseases\"},{\"id\":\"D009190\",\"term\":\"Myelodysplastic Syndromes\"},{\"id\":\"D001855\",\"term\":\"Bone Marrow Diseases\"}]},\"interventionBrowseModule\":{\"meshes\":[{\"id\":\"C539676\",\"term\":\"rEV576 protein, tick\"}]}},\"hasResults\":true}", "media_type": "application/json", "text_derivation": {"extractor_version": "stdlib-json-object-slice-v1", "method": "ctgov-study-json-v1", "raw_asset": {"byte_size": 722762, "media_type": "application/json", "relative_path": "evidence/raw/sha256/5e/5e055f4c38b521ee0b77d8d55c403955f543e6800db21245bd2d1bf36e7b4a14.bin", "sha256": "5e055f4c38b521ee0b77d8d55c403955f543e6800db21245bd2d1bf36e7b4a14"}, "record_selector": {"nct_id": "NCT02591862", "study_index": 10}, "schema_version": "1.0", "text_sha256": "ce3e08ef8cbccdcf66fe46b3e56501ef6523bd2d129744d4ad823c07c2a8b227"}}